    "nts2": [
      {
        "n": "WABI SABI W/ TANA YONAS",
        "s": "2026-09-11T21:00:00+01:00",
        "e": "2026-09-11T22:00:00+01:00",
        "d": "Tana Yonas collects songs like souvenirs, each recalling precious moments found leafing through dusty foreign record shops or catching sonic fragments weathered by time from the radio of bumpy taxi rides. Listen as she delicately guilds together these memories and shares music from lesser known and under represented musical traditions from across the globe and decades.\nFrom the host: \"The artists on this mix, seem to inhabit little worlds of their own. Moving between aquatic ambient music, pastoral folk, cosmic electronics, and quiet experimentation, these recordings feel both ancient and futuristic. Synthesizers dissolve into field recordings, familiar melodies drift into ♾️.\"",
        "j": "TANA YONAS",
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/tana-yonas/episodes/tana-yonas-11th-september-2026",
        "t": "monthly"
      },
      {
        "n": "NTS Guide to: Hard Bop Vol. 1",
        "s": "2026-09-11T22:00:00+01:00",
        "e": "2026-09-12T00:00:00+01:00",
        "d": "The landscape of jazz was altered forever when Charlie Parker electrified the genre, pioneering bebop. When he suddenly passed away in 1955 at the age of 34, many wondered how they could follow him. Some opted to branch off from the bebop style, eschewing the Bird's dense melodic runs and swing influence – they slowed the tempo, and stripped back elements, taking notes from gospel, blues and the R&B sound that was becoming the popular music of the day. \nDespite its less technically demanding style, and slower tempos, the new sound became known as \"hard bop\", because of its gritty, blues-indebted emotion, and tough driving grooves. ",
        "j": "Hard Bop Vol. 1",
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/the-nts-guide-to/episodes/the-nts-guide-to-hard-bop-vol-1-11th-september-2026",
        "t": "weekly"
